  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>The Work Required to Stretch or Compress a Spring</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Suppose it takes a force of \({@force@} \textbf{N}\) (in the negative direction) to compress a spring \({@float(spring_compress)@} \textbf{m}\) from equilibrium position. How much work is done to stretch the spring from \({@float(spring_stretch)@}\textbf{m}\) from the equilibrium</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>First, find the spring constant, \(\textbf{k}\). When \(x=-{@spring_compress@}\) we know \(F(x)=-{@force@}\) so,</p>
<p>\[F(x)=k(x)\]</p>
<p>\[-{@force@}=k(-{@spring_compress@})\]</p>
<p>\[k={@sol2@}\]</p>
<p>and \(F(x)={@sol2@}x\). Then to calculate work, we integrate the force function, obtaining</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
W & =\displaystyle \int_a^b F(x)dx\\
&=\displaystyle \int_0^{@spring_stretch@}{@sol2@}x \,dx\\
&=\displaystyle \big[ {@sol4@} \big]_{0}^{@spring_stretch@}\\
&={@sol5@}\\
& \approx {@decimalplaces(sol5,2)@}\\
\end{align}
\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
